#: ../../guide/installation.md:1
msgid "Installation"
msgstr "Installation"

#: ../../guide/installation.md:3
msgid "VS Code Extension"
msgstr "VS Code Extension"

#: ../../guide/installation.md:5
msgid "Install from the VS Code marketplace:"
msgstr "Install from the VS Code marketplace:"

#: ../../guide/installation.md:7
msgid "Open VS Code"
msgstr "Open VS Code"

#: ../../guide/installation.md:8
#: ../../guide/installation.md:21
msgid "Press `Ctrl+Shift+X` (or `Cmd+Shift+X` on macOS)"
msgstr "Press `Ctrl+Shift+X` (or `Cmd+Shift+X` on macOS)"

#: ../../guide/installation.md:9
#: ../../guide/installation.md:22
msgid "Search for **Language Check**"
msgstr "Search for **Language Check**"

#: ../../guide/installation.md:10
#: ../../guide/installation.md:23
msgid "Click **Install**"
msgstr "Click **Install**"

#: ../../guide/installation.md:12
msgid "On first activation, the extension will prompt you to download the core binary for your platform. You can also install it manually."
msgstr "On first activation, the extension will prompt you to download the core binary for your platform. You can also install it manually."

#: ../../guide/installation.md:14
msgid "VSCodium and other non-Microsoft builds"
msgstr "VSCodium and other non-Microsoft builds"

#: ../../guide/installation.md:16
msgid "VSCodium, Code — OSS, Cursor, Windsurf, and similar builds cannot reach the Microsoft marketplace. The same extension is published to [Open VSX](https://open-vsx.org/extension/KaiErikNiermann/language-check), which those editors query by default:"
msgstr "VSCodium, Code — OSS, Cursor, Windsurf, and similar builds cannot reach the Microsoft marketplace. The same extension is published to [Open VSX](https://open-vsx.org/extension/KaiErikNiermann/language-check), which those editors query by default:"

#: ../../guide/installation.md:20
msgid "Open VSCodium"
msgstr "Open VSCodium"

#: ../../guide/installation.md:25
msgid "Or from the command line:"
msgstr "Or from the command line:"

#: ../../guide/installation.md:31
msgid "The published VSIX is platform-independent — the core binary is fetched separately on first activation, so there is a single artifact for every editor and platform."
msgstr "The published VSIX is platform-independent — the core binary is fetched separately on first activation, so there is a single artifact for every editor and platform."

#: ../../guide/installation.md:34
msgid "If your editor is not wired to Open VSX, grab the `.vsix` from [GitHub Releases](https://github.com/KaiErikNiermann/LangCheck/releases) and install it directly:"
msgstr "If your editor is not wired to Open VSX, grab the `.vsix` from [GitHub Releases](https://github.com/KaiErikNiermann/LangCheck/releases) and install it directly:"

#: ../../guide/installation.md:42
msgid "Offline or proxied installs"
msgstr "Offline or proxied installs"

#: ../../guide/installation.md:44
msgid "The extension downloads `language-check-server` from GitHub Releases the first time it activates. On a machine without direct GitHub access, install the binary yourself (see [CLI Binary](#cli-binary) below) and point the extension at it:"
msgstr "The extension downloads `language-check-server` from GitHub Releases the first time it activates. On a machine without direct GitHub access, install the binary yourself (see [CLI Binary](#cli-binary) below) and point the extension at it:"

#: ../../guide/installation.md:54
msgid "With that set the extension never attempts a download."
msgstr "With that set the extension never attempts a download."

